# Peka — Co-op 2D Platform Puzzler

> Game Design Document (living draft). Filled out as we ideate.
>
> **Decided:** symmetric players + co-op verbs · local couch · mysterious/eerie tone · lightless caverns

---

## 1. Description

A **2D co-op platform game** built around **cooperative puzzles**. Two players
descend together through **one long level** — a system of **lightless caverns**.
The level is designed so it is **impossible to complete solo**: every major
obstacle requires both players acting in coordination.

Tone is **mysterious and eerie** — sparse, atmospheric, told through the
environment rather than text (Limbo / Inside lineage). The pair are small and
vulnerable; the dark is large and unexplained. Something else is down here.

**Core pillars**
- **Forced cooperation** — no section clears without two players.
- **Light is shared & scarce** — the dark is the central pressure (see §2).
- **Puzzle-first platforming** — movement is the verb; the brain-teaser is the challenge.
- **One handcrafted descent** — a single, long, escalating journey downward.
- **Wordless atmosphere** — eerie mood, environmental storytelling, minimal UI.

---

## 2. Cooperation Model — ✅ Symmetric + co-op verbs

Both players control **identical** characters with the **same abilities**. The
dependency comes from **obstacles needing two bodies** and a **single shared
light**, not from asymmetric powers. Either player can do anything — no "main
character."

### ⭐ Core mechanic (proposed): the single light
- There is **one light source** (lantern / flame / crystal) in the world.
- Only **one player carries it at a time**; it can be **handed off** or **set down**.
- The unlit player operates in darkness — limited sight, vulnerable.
- This stays symmetric (the light is a *transferable object*, not a power) while
  forcing handoffs, togetherness, and constant "who takes the light?" decisions.
- [ ] **Confirm this as the core mechanic** (everything below assumes it)

### Cooperative verbs (the teamwork vocabulary) — _draft, to refine_
- **Light handoff / set-down** — pass or place the light; only one carries it.
- **Light as key** — shine on glowing fungi / light-sensitive gates / charge crystals; one holds light steady on a target while the other crosses.
- **Hold-to-open** — one stands on a plate to hold a gate while the other passes.
- **Boost / catch / pull-up** — launch or haul the partner to higher ledges.
- **Counterweight** — both needed on a see-saw, pulley, or balance platform.
- **Lure & protect** — light repels/attracts shadow creatures; one draws them off while the other moves.

- [ ] Lock the final ~4–6 verbs the whole level is built from
- [ ] Decide which verbs are taught early vs. combined late

